S2 scan audit — 10k pending fixture
====================================

BEFORE (pre-S2 query-path scan: correlated EXISTS per in-scope revision)
  SCAN s
  SEARCH sr USING INDEX sqlite_autoindex_source_revision_1 (revision_id=?)
  CORRELATED SCALAR SUBQUERY 1
  SEARCH v USING INDEX idx_view_revision (revision_id=?)
  CORRELATED SCALAR SUBQUERY 2
  SEARCH r USING INDEX idx_run_revision (revision_id=?)
  CORRELATED SCALAR SUBQUERY 3
  SEARCH j USING INDEX idx_job_state (state=?)

BEFORE timing: recompute_pending_coverage(10k) = 6.558s

AFTER (S2 materialized reads)
-- pending page: SELECT revision_id, source_id, missing, has_pending_job FROM revision_coverage WHERE pending = 1 ORDER BY observed_at, revision_id LIMIT ?
   SEARCH revision_coverage USING INDEX idx_cov_pending (pending=?)
-- pending count: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM revision_coverage WHERE pending = 1
   SEARCH revision_coverage USING COVERING INDEX idx_cov_pending (pending=?)
-- hole page: SELECT revision_id, source_id, observed_at, missing, reason FROM coverage_hole ORDER BY observed_at, revision_id LIMIT ?
   SCAN coverage_hole USING INDEX idx_cov_hole_obs
-- hole count: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM coverage_hole
   SCAN coverage_hole USING COVERING INDEX sqlite_autoindex_coverage_hole_1
-- meta version: SELECT value FROM coverage_meta WHERE key = ?
   SEARCH coverage_meta USING INDEX sqlite_autoindex_coverage_meta_1 (key=?)
-- live jobs: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM projection_job WHERE state IN ('pending', 'claimed')
   SEARCH projection_job USING COVERING INDEX idx_cov_job_live (state=?)

AFTER timing: pending page(64) = 1.05ms; full freshness() = 1.92ms
SPEEDUP: 3407x

Budget: query-path freshness < 1.0s at 10k pending (measured ~1ms).
Praxist implication: per-tick freshness cost drops from seconds (eval-loop
dominant) to ~1ms, fitting comfortably in a sub-minute eval loop.
